Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 19:58:28 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 10/19] HIP GCN single-token attention: skip masked blocks;
 leaner mask scan and combine

The sliding-window cache is 7168 cells for 5 slots and a token sees 1024 of them: fully masked blocks
now exit after reading their mask (64 keys a block) and the combine passes over their zero sums. The mask
scan takes one block per bitmap word (15.9 -> 5.5 us at 20k); the combine lists live blocks and loads 8
at a time (18.5 -> 9.0 us). Output identical. MI25, Gemma 4 12B at 20k: 17.4 -> 31.6 t/s.
GGML_CUDA_FA_GCN_SKIP=0 turns the skip off.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01TS8XWm5bp2cWmYvbQ5tTBK
